# Thousand Needles (28-30): Freewind Post and the canyons around it (the Galak centaur, the
# Roguefeather harpies, Highperch, Whitereach Post, the Grimtotem of Darkcloud Pinnacle, Dorn
# Plainstalker's tests), with a first stop at Camp Taurajo and the errands that end in Ratchet and
# Orgrimmar, for a Horde duo.
#
# Built into the addon with:
#   python3 addon/tools/guide_build.py addon/guides/thousand_needles_28_30.guide --db data/forever.sqlite
#
# Research (November 2026): givers, objectives, prerequisites and the places of mobs and objects
# from the game data (data/forever.sqlite), checked against outof.games (Thousand Needles, area 400;
# The Barrens, area 17); RestedXP's and Zygor's routes as a check. The quest list is section 11 of
# addon/guides/horde_1_40_allocation.md.
#
# Starts in Thunder Bluff: Ashenvale (26-28) should end there (it hands in The Sacred Flame, 1195,
#   to Zangen Stonehoof, who then gives 1196 here).
# Carried in (skipped by those who lack them): Calling in the Reserves (5881, from Maggran
#   Earthbinder at Sun Rock Retreat: Stonetalon Mountains (25-26) should take it); for shamans Call
#   of Water (1534, from Brine in the Barrens after Call of Water 1536: The Barrens (24-25) should take
#   it, and Ashenvale (26-28) fill its waterskin at the Ruins of Stardust).
# Left to later guides: Parts for Kravel (1112) for Thousand Needles (33-34); for warriors The
#   Windwatcher (1791) and for shamans Call of Water (63), both for Hillsbrad Foothills (30-32).
# Left out: the Test of Lore (1152, 1154, 6627, 1159, 6628). In this game Braug Dimspirit asks his
#   question (6627) only after you bring him the Legacy of the Aspects (1154) from the Dor'danil Barrow
#   Den in southern Ashenvale, and Parqual Fintallas asks his (6628) only after the book of the Scarlet
#   Monastery (1160, a dungeon). Braug, Dor'danil and Braug again cost about 35 minutes of running for
#   about 4,500 XP, and the chain stops at the dungeon anyway.
#
# The route: Thunder Bluff and a flight to Camp Taurajo; the soldiers on the Dustwallow border and the
# Great Lift down to Freewind Post; a loop north and east (the Galak centaur, Splithoof Hold, Dorn
# Plainstalker, the Gravelsnout kobolds and the alien egg); a loop west (the Roguefeather Den,
# Highperch, Steelsnap, Whitereach Post, the Boiling Pool) and the hearthstone to Thunder Bluff; Camp
# Taurajo and a flight back to Freewind Post; a last loop (Dorn, Darkcloud Pinnacle, Rok'Alim, the
# panther, Whitereach Post); the Shimmering Flats and Gadgetzan; flights to the Crossroads, Ratchet
# and Orgrimmar, where Hillsbrad Foothills (30-32) starts at the zeppelin.

guide Thousand Needles (28-30)
faction horde
levels 28 30
carry 529 546 567 1534 5881
leave 63 529 546 567 1112 1791
next Hillsbrad Foothills (30-32)

# Thunder Bluff ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

map Thunder Bluff
accept 1196
tip Zangen Stonehoof stands on the central rise. He has this for those who brought him the moonwell water (The Sacred Flame) in Ashenvale.
accept 1131
tip Melor Stonehoof is on Hunter Rise.
bind 6746
tip Set your hearthstone here: it brings you back from the far west of Thousand Needles halfway through the guide.
fly "Camp Taurajo" npc 2995
tip No flight path to Camp Taurajo? Ride east out of Mulgore instead: the camp is just past the gate into the Barrens.

# Camp Taurajo and the south of the Barrens ----------------------------------------------------------

map The Barrens
accept 97250
accept 1153
tip Tatternack Steelforge has this for those who did his Weapons of Choice. You come back here halfway through to hand both in.
turnin 1534 only shaman
tip Brine sits on top of the hill south of Camp Taurajo, by the road to the Great Lift.
accept 220 only shaman
tip Keep the Vial of Purest Water: Islen Waterseer near Ratchet wants it at the end of the guide.
do 97250
tip The Alliance soldiers stand a short way east of Brine's hill, at the edge of Dustwallow Marsh. The Outraged Pillager is an elite of level 23: easy for the two of you. They come back about six minutes after they die.
turnin 5881
tip Grish Longrunner guards the top of the Great Lift, at the southern tip of the Barrens.
accept 4542
tip Brave Moonhorn stands beside him. Take the lift down; don't step off before it reaches the bottom.

